WEBVTT

00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:30.274
he said, "then, by analogy with 'artist,'

00:01:30.274 --> 00:01:34.214
we may form 'scientist.'"

00:01:34.214 --> 00:01:36.843
This was the first time the word scientist

00:01:36.843 --> 00:01:38.697
was uttered in public,

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:42.293
only 179 years ago.

00:01:42.293 --> 00:01:45.438
I first found out about this confrontation when I was in graduate school,

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.482
and it kind of blew me away.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:49.666
I mean, how could the word scientist

00:01:49.666 --> 00:01:53.155
not have existed until 1833?

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.346
What were scientists called before?

00:01:55.346 --> 00:01:58.671
What had changed to make a new name necessary

00:01:58.671 --> 00:02:01.801
precisely at that moment?